From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Seer: the sidebar lists Songs first

The sidebar lists Songs first, as the user preferred in the earlier version (the patch
from that version does not apply cleanly to the current code, so the change is redone here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/ui/src/layout/Menu.jsx b/ui/src/layout/Menu.jsx
index 0a9b14d..cbc194c 100644
--- a/ui/src/layout/Menu.jsx
+++ b/ui/src/layout/Menu.jsx
@@ -132,7 +132,10 @@ const Menu = ({ dense = false }) => {
           renderAlbumMenuItemLink(type, albumLists[type]),
         )}
       </SubMenu>
-      {resources.filter(subItems(undefined)).map(renderResourceMenuItemLink)}
+      {resources
+        .filter(subItems(undefined))
+        .sort((a, b) => (a.name === 'song' ? -1 : b.name === 'song' ? 1 : 0))
+        .map(renderResourceMenuItemLink)}
       {config.devSidebarPlaylists && open ? (
         <>
           <Divider />
